---
description: Resolve the actual route-authority goal through semantic composition and exact native authorities.
args:
  goal: string
returns: RouteResult
---
Resolve the actual evidence question using current native route authority and the requested origin ceiling. Discovery, preflight eligibility, approval and execution are distinct. A route being acquirable is not an already held grant, and a permitted operation is not automatically requested. Compose an authority inquiry, any needed actual selected read, and a conclusion from real feedback. Do not broaden the origin ceiling or substitute an unrequested shell, network operation or historical copy.

Compare only the sources the user actually asks to compare. Explain missing authority or unavailable evidence honestly; never present a preflight as a completed read. Retain a private review only when requested and natively admitted. Return actual requested findings, real readback and optional retained artifact.
